kosha monotone-map

  -- a function that preserves order: if a ≤ b then f(a) ≤ f(b).
  -- every pipeline tantra is monotone: triples are only added, never removed.
  -- this is the key property that guarantees fixpoint existence (Knaster-Tarski).
  -- monotone endomorphism on a complete lattice has a least fixpoint.

  "algebra-varga-karma"
  "morphism-swarupa endomorphism-abheda"
  "partial-order-sthita lattice-sthita"
  "structure-yukta order-preserving-swarupa"
  "fixed-point-siddha"

done
